sentences.l:
for I myself gave these clothes, such as you describe,
having folded them out of the chamber, and I put on a shining brooch
for that man, to be an ornament;

for indeed any woman laments, having lost a man of another sort,
her wedded one, by whom she bore children, having mingled in love,
than Odysseus, whom they say to be like the gods.

for unerringly I will tell you, and will not hide it,
how already of Odysseus’s return I heard
near, in the rich land of the Thesprotian men,
alive;

but his trusty companions
he lost, and his hollow ship on the wine-faced open-sea,
as he came from the island of Thrinacia;

So he indeed thus is safe, and will come now
very near, nor any longer far from his dear ones and his fatherland
will he be away for long;
